  "optimized_engine_benchmark_note": "scripts/benchmark-git-refresh.py --baseline-git HEAD --runs 7 --repos 200 with BENCH_CONCURRENCY=10 (the app's ScanConfig default). Stage split at -O, 200 repositories: coreStatus 353.2 ms, discovery 56.7 ms, merge 0.4 ms of a 411.8 ms incremental refresh.",
  "notes": "CPU figures are RUSAGE_SELF + RUSAGE_CHILDREN increments over the measured refresh window, so they include the Git child processes. The candidate completes the same 200 git status calls; it does so with more overlap and less idle waiting, so window CPU rises while wall time falls. The optimized engine benchmark below measures RUSAGE_SELF only. refresh_result_signature covers repository name, branch, status, file counts and pin state, not the whole payload."
}
